{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_22d5c6340e728f553e5e992f22048e97181d9668881f11cfb8792ebfac3c00a5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_711398fc53aa5fac860659823aa7681c0288ec0f7501cacdfa6de0b6254ae0d2","slc_7e0d32e4229e58fdfcf124e5c4a9f6dc11118c52f09e910a3afd18685b2f4841","slc_f81ec5c113912ec6706a53ad488f31a608b188a16105c4a32ac4cc8ab9cdabdc"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"Per-agent model routing uses Cursor's model: frontmatter field; the default is composer-2.5-fast, with Sokka and Iroh on claude-opus-4-8-thinking-high and Zuko on gemini-3.1-pro.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_28235d4db184be1f31a9edae28411c37017f841f75d732636de60e280a4979d8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e9f53ead37930a1a612bf4d968f8ecd1fce7f0ed509c57b94f0428768624e2e6","slc_f0750df42852a4ad9d185caddf74a4896ac4ad63d54b73024ae97966d3f2dbda"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"The installer supports user (default ~/.cursor) and project (./.cursor) scopes, plus --claude/--codex cross-tool installs, --dry-run, --force, --uninstall, and --disable/--enable orchestration flags.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2c206cd08c2fabaeead0b2d3451a0e6333cf7a9d79f545d6a15205347648ff82","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c80bd5c02cb612820afdee25de9925f9fa51e10cb33a1caea95c4bbca573dde8"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo and run bash install.sh (or install.ps1 on Windows) to install from source; changes to agents, rules, commands, or hooks take effect after reinstalling.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_50699e2f38d65fcdd6fd4838f1ea70160d72f821a047ca6018945507c6ceacdd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0bf2ef1aab8dffc2a39a21a2dcdf7d6f2a61f3ac673d4d0f9b93c34b0e1b4aa0","slc_4aa6dd7c599217ff96ad12dc6539a47472b97bb26f36c1b3131c3f8b968ede59"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"On Cursor 3.4+ a two-tier swarm pattern applies: coordinators (Aang, Sokka, Katara, Appa) spawn worker agents (Toph, Momo) as leaf nodes with max depth 2; Zuko is root-only.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_57651503d8478abd2c8bef4b5f0f2dc31262c0eeb8dbc9da2b1fd86d722e3671","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2c725c4266a0f2a10fbe355342010001cdd705a5ae71780e6a6363fc20115c38","slc_3eca53ca0c37df9aabe701e9a6313e26bd7bc1bd6bcad4366e3187dbb0329218"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"A '/cactus-juice' swarm mode decomposes requests into 5-10 independent single-file micro-tasks and spawns up to 10 parallel fast-model subagents, with the root collecting and verifying results.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_57bb1ec049a4b97399cd70947302af05245d4e61bccf10c0e369a52d2df1918f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_20c4907cf6accbac622684068ffb7930bc0fe5ae5b2341cafd2f2dee44b05685"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"A permissions.json auto-review policy auto-runs safe calls (lints, tests, builds, read-only git) and holds risky ones (destructive filesystem, history rewrites, credential access, outbound network) for review.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6da49be344dcd27065b82a9c85f22c10cca84912cc0b39e3a9b56eb6ed7fc0b4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5e3af4ae9d46f7205feca92929f72f005931ddaae8ff7dfc9f5e8addda18328f"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"The README states hooks and auto-review are best-effort and not a security boundary, reducing footguns and approval spam without replacing real sandboxing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7cb6ed239ff8b943c9be60f56704dec43f47c49a25732229f61c4032a72f9b78","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor@5bad458bff4c snapshot 0945cff458e1ce6e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_13c2e9a355d2a86f3a64767a0c70e16a2884e6cf953476bef7cf23beefef8a82"],"source_ids":["src_448adfbd88f35385863558a3cbcfbc92"],"text":"The orchestrator rule makes the root thread a pure dispatcher whose only permitted tools are Task, TodoWrite, AskQuestion, and SwitchMode, delegating all work to specialist agents.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
